{"run_id": "20260816T233639-hepkg-48572", "qid": "gen-conceptset-bebbd2f4", "repeat": 1, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "92159134c9c3", "git_sha": "be3072a-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate a background using Data-driven matrix method?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql", "merged_entities"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 30 distinct analyses that estimate a background using a method related to the Data-driven matrix method. \n\nTo provide more context, these 30 analyses include a variety of specific methods, such as:\n- Data-driven matrix method\n- Data-driven fake-factor method\n- Data-driven tight-to-loose ratio method\n- Data-driven fake-factor/matrix method for FNP lepton estimation\n- ABCD (matrix) data-driven background estimation\n- Multidimensional ABCD reweighting technique\n- Data-driven \\( t\\bar{t} \\) estimation from \\( e\\mu \\) events\n- Data-driven \\( N_{\\mathrm{jets}} \\)-dependent correction to \\( VV \\) simulation\n- Data-driven normalization from unconstrained fit parameter in signal region\n- Data-driven multijet estimate via \\(\\Delta\\phi_{\\min}\\) control region and exponential extrapolation\n- Mixed-data sample method\n- Control-region data-driven normalization\n- Discrete profiling method for data-driven background modeling\n- Data-driven charge-misidentification probability method\n- Data-driven multi-jet-enriched control-region template-fit method\n- Data-driven fake-rate method using multijet control regions\n- Data-driven jet-smearing (resolution-function) technique\n- Data-driven fake-muon control-region method\n- Tight-to-loose data-driven nonprompt-lepton estimation method\n- Data-driven misidentification/prompt-rate (fake rate) method\n- Direct MC simulation prediction (no data-driven correction)\n- Data-driven normalization from control region fit (CR_ttbar), simultaneous with signal region\n- Data-driven normalisation via simultaneous profile-likelihood fit in dedicated control regions\n- MC simulation normalised to data in dedicated control regions (partially data-driven)\n- Data-driven normalisation in kinematically similar control regions\n\nEach of these methods is a variant or extension of the Data-driven matrix method, and they are used across various analyses in the literature.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2403.01556", "2404.06204", "2405.18661", "2407.10549", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2604.21670", "2604.27044", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Data-driven matrix method", "kind": "background_method"}, "rows": 82, "error": null, "seconds": 78.445}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "background_uses_method", "object_set": "set_1_kept"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.061}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hepkg:background_method:abcd_data_driven_crs", "hepkg:background_method:cr_normalisation_fit", "hepkg:background_method:data_driven_fake_factor", "hepkg:background_method:data_driven_gjets_randomized_id", "hepkg:background_method:data_driven_nonprompt_control_sample", "hepkg:background_method:discrete_profiling", "hepkg:background_method:mc-simulation-estimate", "hepkg:method:abcd-method", "hepkg:method:abcd-reweighting", "hepkg:method:charge_misid_data_driven", "hepkg:method:continuum_data_fit", "hepkg:method:control_region_data", "hepkg:method:control_region_normalization", "hepkg:method:core-p