{"run_id": "20260816T233639-hepkg-48572", "qid": "gen-conceptset-436046a1", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "92159134c9c3", "git_sha": "be3072a-dirty", "question": "Which analyses define a region requiring Primary vertex (PV)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses define a region requiring a Primary vertex (PV):\n\n- **2004.01678**: Preselection region (m_llj < 250 GeV) and Signal Region (SR)\n- **2009.14537**: Preselection region (opposite-charge same-flavor dilepton, Z-veto, low p_T^ll)\n- **2012.01581**: Common dijet/SV preselection region (Table 2) and Final signal region (Region H)\n- **2107.12553**: Baseline preselection common to all signal regions (Table 6) and 12 non-overlapping signal regions categorized in N_H, N_jets, p_T^miss (Table 8)\n- **2304.08962**: Signal region (SR): tight vertex, m4mu<11 GeV, ΔR<0.25\n- **2401.07090**: Electron channel baseline preselection (B+ mass 4.7-5.7 GeV, prior to q^2 binning)\n- **2403.01556**: Generic emerging-jet signal region (>=2 tagged EJs)\n- **2404.06204**: Detector-level signal regions for W -> e nu, W -> mu nu, Z -> ee, and Z -> mu mu selections\n- **2508.13900**: Common preselection region (all channels)\n\nThese are the distinct papers that define regions requiring a Primary vertex (PV).", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2207.12246", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2309.14442", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2401.07090", "2402.08486", "2403.01556", "2404.0